---
description: General project coding standards
alwaysApply: true
---
- Prefer small composable modules.
- Use descriptive names and explicit domain types.
- Avoid unnecessary any.
- Handle errors explicitly.
- Avoid hidden global state.
- Check existing dependencies before adding new ones.
- Keep components accessible.
- Avoid unnecessary Next.js client components.
- Keep server-only crawler/browser code out of the browser bundle.
